You are assigning OCR-extracted words to webpage sections.

You have been given:
1. A list of named sections with descriptions (from the ground-truth page)
2. The full OCR word list from the GROUND-TRUTH image (words with fractional y positions)
3. The full OCR word list from the AGENT-GENERATED image (words with fractional y positions)

Your job is to assign every word in BOTH word lists to the most appropriate section label.
If a word does not belong to any section, assign it to "unassigned".

SECTIONS:
{% for section in sections %}
- label: "{{ section.label }}" ({{ section.type }})
  description: {{ section.description }}
{% endfor %}

GROUND-TRUTH WORD LIST (format: "word [y=0.NN]"):
{{ gt_words }}

AGENT WORD LIST (format: "word [y=0.NN]"):
{{ agent_words }}

Rules:
- Use the section descriptions as anchors — assign words that clearly belong to a section's content
- Use the fractional y position as a secondary signal — words for the same section should cluster vertically
- Assign the same label to corresponding words in both lists (e.g. "Early Bird" belongs to tickets_step in both)
- If a word could belong to multiple sections, use the description content match over the y position
- Every word must be assigned to exactly one label or "unassigned"
- Output ONLY a JSON object in the exact shape below, no prose, no markdown fences

Output shape:
{
  "gt_sections":    {"nav": ["word1", "word2", ...], "tickets_step": ["Early", "Bird", "$20", ...], "unassigned": [...]},
  "agent_sections": {"nav": ["word1", "word2", ...], "tickets_step": ["Early", "Bird", "$25", ...], "unassigned": [...]}
}
